{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQkvsxVdrGbTYavLkEr3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Round 9 review: changes requested.** There are three medium blockers (N1–N3) and four low follow-ups (N4–N7). `draft-check` accepted the draft below.\n\n| Finding | Severity | Defect |\n|---|---|---|\n| N1 | medium, blocker | `artifact-check --strict` and `surface-check --strict` fail: the spec claims `delegation.json`, but the commits that change it have no `POSE-Spec` trailer. |\n| N2 | medium, blocker | The new line-joining can cut or widen a sealed limit without reporting it, and can take a reason from a later paragraph. |\n| N3 | medium, blocker | An ADR that cites the spec only by its dated file link no longer has to name the spec's limits. |\n| N4 | low, follow-up | Skipping of code blocks and comments is incomplete. |\n| N5 | low, follow-up | Text output omits `within-limit` findings. |\n| N6 | low, follow-up | One brief step still says any other finding stays open. |\n| N7 | low, within L1 | The reason check accepts placeholder words. |\n\n- **Accepted limits:** I found L1 and L2 justified. In the code and its tests, `within-limit` approves only a sealed limit id with a reason, and the new fields are omitted when empty, so plans without limits keep their digests.\n- **Tests:** the focused tests and `go vet` on `pose` and `cli` passed.\n- **Sandbox limits:** `go test ./...` did not pass here. The failures I inspected came from directory ownership restrictions, and some packages also hit timeouts. `validate --strict --module pose-mcp` was cancelled at my 420s bound. I did not run the repository-wide `validate --strict`. Both `validate` entries therefore rely on sealed evidence.\n- **Cleanup:** `go clean -cache` and the removal of `go-build*` leftovers under `GOTMPDIR` both succeeded.\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md\",\"line\":72,\"summary\":\"The spec declares 'modified: .pose/policy/delegation.json' (added by b5296a37), but the commits in the range that change it (7bf729e0, 3e1f03cf) carry no POSE-Spec trailer. 'artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict' and 'surface-check --strict' both exit 1 with error action-mismatch on that path, so two required tools fail. Attribute the exact revisions to the spec or correct the claim, then rerun both checks.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":99,\"summary\":\"The continuation-line fix reads entry boundaries wrongly (probed through a test overlay). (a) A wrapped line starting with '#' ('see issue\\\\n  #42 only on Linux') is taken as a heading: the limit is sealed cut at the first line, with no problem reported. (b) A nested '- only on Linux' sub-bullet is reported by lint, but the plan discards problems (line 134) and seals the limit without its qualifier. (c) A later non-indented paragraph after a blank line, or a following '* L2: ...' bullet, is appended into L1 and changes the sealed limit (L2 vanishes). (d) '- L1: no reason here', a blank line, then 'Some unrelated note. Accepted because other words follow.' now passes with no problem: the ready check accepts a reason borrowed from a later paragraph, which R4 and the round 4 rule refuse. End an entry where its Markdown list item ends, treat only real headings as headings, refuse (and do not seal) what cannot be read whole, with tests.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":1200,\"summary\":\"Regression from the N4 fix: the whole-slug pattern refuses a preceding '-', so an ADR that cites the spec only by its file link, for example '[it](../specs/2026-11-25-limited.md)', is no longer a citing ADR and the ready check demands no limit from it (probe returned no failure; the directory form and 'spec:limited' still demand L1). Dated flat files are how this repository's ADRs link specs, some by link alone with a descriptive label (.pose/adr/2026-09-21-federated-roadmap-acceptance-with-local-evidence-authority.md:6), so R4 goes unenforced for them. Recognise the dated spec path as a citation, with a test.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":74,\"summary\":\"Fence and comment skipping is incomplete (probed). Any ``` or ~~~ prefix toggles one flag, so an example inside a four-backtick block or a ~~~ block holding ``` is sealed as a real limit; a 4-space indented code example is sealed too. A line starting with inline ```a``` or a literal unterminated '<!--' earlier in the body silently drops every later limit, with no problem and a passing lint (lint strips only closed comments); a comment written in backticks inside a limit is removed from its sealed text. A '* L1:' bullet alone is silently ignored.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/governance_stats.go\",\"line\":132,\"summary\":\"within_limit_findings is counted and present in JSON, but the text output of the governance stats prints findings, accepted_risk, resolved, open and wont_fix without it, so the printed buckets still do not add up; review-check and closeout-check text still do not show within-limit findings, which the spec constraint wants visible in the closeout.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\",\"line\":563,\"summary\":\"review-brief/11 still says in the conclusion step that a follow-up with action, owner and review_by is an accepted risk and 'any other finding stays open', which is false for a follow-up with a sealed limit (rule (m) states the exception only to rule (i)).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N7\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"limit\":\"L1\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":49,\"summary\":\"Carried from R8-N6: the lexical reason gate accepts placeholder words. Inside L1: it is a format gate over text the implementer writes, and the sealed brief shows that text for the reviewer to judge and dispute.\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R8-N1\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Plain wrapped lines are now kept (accepted_limits.go:99-101; TestAcceptedLimitsReadWrappedEntriesAndSkipExamples passes), but probes still cut a limit at a '#' continuation or a nested sub-bullet, and the new joining over-reads later paragraphs; see N2.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R8-N2\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Simple fenced blocks and closed HTML comments are skipped (accepted_limits.go:72-80, test passes); probes still seal examples from nested or mixed fences and indented code; see N4.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R8-N3\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"review_brief.go adds rule (m) and lists limit among the finding fields; this brief shows both; TestTheCurrentBriefListsTheAcceptedLimits passes in the focused go test run. A residual sentence in another step is N6.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R8-N4\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"lintspec.go:1200 matches the slug as a whole name; the limited-other case of TestReadyCheckJudgesAcceptedLimits passes. The regression it introduces is N3.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R8-N5\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"governance_outcomes.go:455-458 counts within-limit and its test passes, but governance_stats.go:132 does not print the bucket and no review-check or closeout-check text change shows the findings; see N5.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R8-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"accepted_limits.go:49 still counts letter runs; TestAnAcceptedLimitNeedsWordsAsItsReason is unchanged in rule. Recorded within L1 as N7.\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"Read accepted_limits.go, its tests and the lint test; the range diff of lintspec, governance_outcomes, review_brief, review_bundle, review_closeout, review_conclusions, review_plan and review_rounds; the round 8 to subject diff including manuals and template digest; the spec; draft parsing, round accounting, finding decision gate, obligation and legacy evaluation consumers of finding dispositions; schemas. Probed the parser and the ADR check with go test -overlay files in TMPDIR. Ran the focused tests (pass), go vet on pose and cli (pass), go test ./... (sandbox failures from directory ownership and sockets, and timeouts; other packages listed ok), the planned pose checks, and a time-bounded validate that was cancelled.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Examined L1 and L2. L1 is an accepted risk about implementer-written limits, mitigated by the brief listing them as data and by open findings blocking approval. L2 is verified: both plan digests cover accepted_limits. Neither is broader than its text; parser defects that alter a sealed limit are outside them (N2).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\"rationale\":\"accepted_limits and limit are omitempty in the plan, bundle, both digests, drafts and attestations, and the digest test compares with the legacy bundle contract. within_limit_findings is an added field. Earlier brief templates stay selectable. The /11 text changed after round 8 was briefed with it; the template is unreleased and that run concluded changes-requested.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-9d93fd07c4704048\",\"rationale\":\"D1 and D2 address the stated cause, reviews that cannot converge without a declared environment: limits are sealed before review, classified by a distinct disposition requiring a sealed id and a reason, and disputable. The structural assessment reports no deltas to map.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N6\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the ready check and decision gate messages: each names the limit, ADR or finding and the fault. Silent parser cases and missing text output are reported separately as N2, N4 and N5.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"within-limit approves only an id present in the sealed bundle with a non-blank reason; blocker findings with a limit stay open; limit text is rendered as one quoted line with backticks neutralised; ADRs are read as regular bounded files without following links.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A spec section, two omitted-when-empty fields, one disposition and a lint check are close to the smallest sufficient change; a round cap would approve unreviewed work. The choice fails if sealed limits can differ from the declared ones, which N2 and N4 address.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 1: error action-mismatch on .pose/policy/delegation.json (N1).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-9d93fd07c4704048\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, no deltas.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the HTTP consumer gaps shown are unrelated to this change.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; scan reports itself incomplete because of two unreadable old specs.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Needs the completed review.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\"rationale\":\"The command run here exits 1 with error action-mismatch (N1); the cited sealed ref is reachability evidence, not a pass of this command.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Relies on sealed evidence. Full strict validation was not completed here: the module run was cancelled at the time bound, with sandbox failures from directory ownership.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Relies on sealed evidence. The sandbox run was cancelled at 420s (exit 124); the failures inspected came from directory ownership restrictions.\"}\n ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":158766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e2183e71-ebed-4751-91f2-96b9f85ec55c","timestamp":"2026-11-26T02:34:32.127Z","request_id":"req_011ChQkvskbRnPQUtPn4tGYo"}
